<title>JAPAN: Japan May cocoa bean imports down 8.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May cocoa bean imports down 8.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in May totalled 5,073 tonnes, down by 8.8 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			May 97	  Apr 97	 May 96</p>
<p> Total		5,073	   4,305	  5,563</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		4,115	   3,827	  3,971</p>
<p> Venezuela	    406	     549	    423</p>
<p> Ecuador		331	     386	    390</p>
<p> Brazil		 120	     474	    291</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first five months of calendar 1997 were 28,032 tonnes against 22,690 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			May 97	  Apr 97	May 96</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	  190	     130	    100</p>
<p> Cocoa butter     1,230	   1,514	  1,558</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	 662	     736	  1,458</p>
<p> Chocolate</p>
<p>  confectionery     668	     825	    825</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
